Intuition
We need to place N queens on an N × N chessboard such that no two queens attack each other.

Since queens can attack horizontally, vertically, and diagonally, we need to ensure that every queen is placed in a safe position.

We can solve this using backtracking by placing one queen in each row and exploring all possible column positions.

Approach
Initialize an N × N board with '.' representing empty cells.
Start placing queens from the first row.
For each row, try placing a queen in every column.
Before placing a queen, check whether the position is safe using the isSafe() method.
Check the column above.
Check the upper-right diagonal.
Check the upper-left diagonal.
If the position is safe:
Place the queen ('Q').
Recursively move to the next row.
Backtrack by removing the queen ('.') after the recursive call.
If all N rows are successfully filled, increment the count.
Return the total number of valid arrangements.
Since we are filling the board from top to bottom, we only need to check the upper column and upper diagonals.

Complexity
Time complexity: (O(N! \times N)) — We explore possible queen placements row by row. Each safety check takes (O(N)) time.
Space complexity: (O(N^2)) — For the N × N board, with an additional (O(N)) recursion stack.
Code
class Solution {
    static int count = 0;

    public int totalNQueens(int n) {
        count = 0;
        char[][] board = new char[n][n];

        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            Arrays.fill(board[i], '.');
        }

        helper(board, 0);
        return count;
    }

    public void helper(char[][] board, int row) {
        if (row == board.length) {
            count++;
            return;
        }

        for (int j = 0; j < board.length; j++) {
            if (isSafe(board, row, j)) {
                board[row][j] = 'Q';

                helper(board, row + 1);

                board[row][j] = '.';
            }
        }
    }

    public static boolean isSafe(char[][] board, int row, int col) {

        // Check upper column
        for (int i = row - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
            if (board[i][col] == 'Q') {
                return false;
            }
        }

        // Check upper-right diagonal
        for (int i = row - 1, j = col + 1;
             i >= 0 && j < board.length; i--, j++) {
            if (board[i][j] == 'Q') {
                return false;
            }
        }

        // Check upper-left diagonal
        for (int i = row - 1, j = col - 1;
             i >= 0 && j >= 0; i--, j--) {
            if (board[i][j] == 'Q') {
                return false;
            }
        }

        return true;
    }
}
